  "notes": [
    "periodic tick work is driven by capture time, not by tick count: this run pushed 12069 s of capture through in 30.0 s of wall clock, a 402x speedup, so the engine did about 402 times the periodic analysis per wall second that a live link at this packet rate would ask for",
    "the capture set was replayed 1.5 times end to end, each pass offset forward in capture time; repeated sessions then look periodic at the capture period, which raises beacon evaluation cost, so any alert from a looped run is a replay artefact, not a detection",
